cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LayaMed, please cite it with the metadata below."
title: "LayaMed: live diagnostic evidence while writing a clinical case"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Computational Systems Biology Laboratory (CSBL-USP)"
  - given-names: "Luís"
    family-names: "Espinosa"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/csbl-usp/LayaMed"
abstract: >-
  A step-by-step guide and local interface that show, while a clinical case is
  being written, the probabilities of a Laya encoder fine-tuned on 4 acute
  abdominal diseases (appendicitis, cholecystitis, pancreatitis and
  diverticulitis), with an out-of-scope detector and recalibration for partial
  cases. Teaching example with synthetic cases; not a medical device.
keywords:
  - clinical NLP
  - medical AI
  - encoder
  - calibration
  - out-of-distribution detection
  - acute abdomen
